From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yodaliu <yodaliu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:32:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] input: qpnp-power-on: always log PMIC key events

Reconstructed from the stock FiiO M21 FW 1.1.0 module by disassembly
comparison; the rebuilt module matches the stock one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/input/misc/qpnp-power-on.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/qpnp-power-on.c b/drivers/input/misc/qpnp-power-on.c
index 69bb7b130ee..0f334807d24 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/qpnp-power-on.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/qpnp-power-on.c
@@ -1030,7 +1030,7 @@ static int qpnp_pon_input_dispatch(struct qpnp_pon *pon, u32 pon_type)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	pr_debug("PMIC input: code=%d, status=0x%02X\n", cfg->key_code,
+	printk("PMIC input: code=%d, status=0x%02X\n", cfg->key_code,
 		pon_rt_sts);
 	key_status = pon_rt_sts & pon_rt_bit;
 
